This is a conceptual organization, not a restriction on the actual implementation.

The user must be able to search across all supported categories.

## Selection Behavior

When the user selects a class:

Display its members and metadata.

When the user selects an object:

Display its fields, values, methods, and related objects.

When the user selects a field:

Display its type, modifiers, current value, and available operations.

When the user selects a method:

Display its signature, parameters, return type, and an option to execute it.

When the user selects a service:

Display its implementation information, interfaces, available objects, Binder associations, and supported operations.

When the user selects a Binder endpoint:

Display its descriptor, available interface information, proxy information, and supported transaction metadata.

The UI must support expanding and collapsing elements without losing the current navigation context.

