# 5. Interactive Runtime Operations

The Explorer must not be read-only.

It must provide an operation layer that allows the user to interact with supported runtime elements.

## Field Operations

For an accessible field, support:

- Read value.
- Display value.
- Edit value.
- Apply modification.
- Restore previous value when possible.
- Display modification result.
- Show errors.

Support common types:

- String
- Boolean
- Byte
- Short
- Int
- Long
- Float
- Double
- Char
- Enum
- Primitive arrays
- Object references
- Supported collections

For complex objects, provide a navigation option instead of forcing them into primitive input fields.

## Method Operations

For each supported method:

- Show method name.
- Show complete signature.
- Show declaring class.
- Show modifiers.
- Show parameter types.
- Show return type.
- Show exceptions.
- Identify static or instance method.
- Resolve available target instances.
- Provide an execution action.

The user must be able to navigate from the method to its declaring class and related objects.

## Constructor Operations

Allow users to:

- Inspect constructors.
- Select a constructor.
- Explore its parameters.
- Provide input values.
- Construct an instance when supported.
- Register the resulting object.
- Open the created object in the Explorer.

