# 21. Mandatory Engineering Rules

1. Build a real working project, not just architecture diagrams or pseudocode.
2. Do not create fake functionality or placeholder implementations presented as completed features.
3. Do not confuse DEX class discovery with loaded class discovery.
4. Do not claim full heap visibility unless the selected integration supports it.
5. Do not assume ordinary AAR integration provides system_server access.
6. Keep Application Runtime and Platform Runtime integrations separate.
7. Use capability-based APIs.
8. Keep Reflection integrated into the Explorer.
9. Keep the Runtime Runner integrated into the same navigation experience.
10. Every operation must return a structured result.
11. Every object must have a process-aware identity.
12. Avoid blocking critical threads.
13. Implement error handling at provider boundaries.
14. Keep the SDK modular and reusable.
15. Write documentation for every public API.
16. Provide tests for every core capability.
17. Maintain compatibility across Android versions through runtime capability detection.
18. Prioritize a functional end-to-end workflow over implementing many incomplete modules.

